# A reduce action names its rule in a 16-bit table cell, so a grammar may
# expand into at most 32766 rules. Each alternative of `top` expands into
# 2^14 = 16384 rules (one per combination of its optional rule references),
# within the per-alternative limit; together they pass the grammar's.
# error: too_many_rules.grammar:19:8:
# error: the grammar expands into more than 32766 rules
@lexer
tokens
    a
    b
    eof
    err
'a' → a
'b' → b
. → err

@parser
top! = A [r1] [r2] [r3] [r4] [r5] [r6] [r7] [r8] [r9] [r10] [r11] [r12] [r13] [r14]
     | B [r1] [r2] [r3] [r4] [r5] [r6] [r7] [r8] [r9] [r10] [r11] [r12] [r13] [r14]
r1 = A A
r2 = A A
r3 = A A
r4 = A A
r5 = A A
r6 = A A
r7 = A A
r8 = A A
r9 = A A
r10 = A A
r11 = A A
r12 = A A
r13 = A A
r14 = A A
